<p>
    The Upc-E barcode is a compact version of the UPC-A barcode symbology that encodes 6 numeric digits.
    It is commonly used for small packages and products where space is limited.
    The Upc-E barcode is designed to be a more condensed version of the UPC-A barcode, allowing for a smaller footprint while still providing product identification and inventory management capabilities.
    As Upc-A barcode, you can only customize the height and width of the bars by setting the <code>ModuleHeight</code> and <code>ModuleWidth</code> parameters respectively in the <code>UpcESymbology</code> component.
</p>

<div style="height: 400px">
    <FluentStack Height="100%" VerticalGap="50" Orientation="Orientation.Vertical">
        <FluentStack HorizontalGap="8px">
            <FluentTextInput Label="Value to encode as barcode"
                             @bind-Value="Value"
                             MinLength="6"
                             MaxLength="6" />
        </FluentStack>
        
        <FluentCxBarcode Value="@Value">
            <UpcESymbology />
        </FluentCxBarcode>
    </FluentStack>
</div>

@code {
    private string Value { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
